cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "EGN: Equivariant Geodesic Networks on the SPD manifold"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Khan
    given-names: Md Raihan
    email: kraihan918@gmail.com
    affiliation: "North Western University, Bangladesh"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kraihan/EGN"
url: "https://github.com/kraihan/EGN"
abstract: >-
  EGN is a deep classifier on the manifold of symmetric positive definite
  matrices. Every intermediate representation is an exact SPD matrix under the
  affine-invariant Riemannian metric, constrained parameters are updated by
  retraction, and the spectral operators are differentiable through repeated
  eigenvalues. The package exposes a scikit-learn style estimator that infers
  matrix size, channel count and class vocabulary from the data, so one object
  applies to EEG, radar, skeleton and imaging descriptors without dataset
  specific code.
keywords:
  - riemannian-geometry
  - spd-manifold
  - covariance
  - deep-learning
  - pytorch
  - eeg
  - brain-computer-interface
